    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Following the abdication of the popular King Edward VIII of Britain, his brother Bertie became King George VI. Bertie suffered from a debilitating speech impediment leading his wife, Queen Elizabeth to seek the help of the eccentric Australian speech therapist, Lionel Logue. This re-enactment of true events tells how Logue helped the King overcome his stuttering at a critical time when World War II was imminent.</marc:subfield>
